datarium: licensing of code and data
=====================================

Package code
------------
The package code (the R documentation sources and package
infrastructure) is licensed under GPL-2, as stated in the DESCRIPTION
"License" field.

Data sets
---------
Except where noted below, the data sets in this package are dedicated
to the public domain by the package author under the Creative Commons
CC0 1.0 Universal Public Domain Dedication
(https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/).

Most of these data sets were created by the author -- simulated for
teaching, each with a fixed random seed (see the data set's help page).
Some are reshaped or expanded from base R data sets or from publicly
reported summary tables -- for example "AirPassengersDf" and
"titanic.raw" from base R's "AirPassengers" and "Titanic",
"housetasks.raw" from a published table, and "renalstone" from Hazra
and Gogtay (2016). Each such origin is credited in the data set's help
page ("@source"). The CC0 dedication covers this package's own
contribution -- the compilation, simulation, reshaping and case-level
recovery; the underlying statistical facts are not themselves subject
to copyright.

heartdisease
------------
The "heartdisease" data set is redistributed from the UCI Machine
Learning Repository under the Creative Commons Attribution 4.0
International licence (CC BY 4.0,
https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/). When using it, please
attribute the source and cite Janosi, Steinbrunn, Pfisterer and Detrano
(1989), Heart Disease, UCI Machine Learning Repository,
doi:10.24432/C52P4X. See "?heartdisease" for the full attribution.
